<title>FRANCE: Iraqi wheat deal imminent - French trade.</title>
<headline>Iraqi wheat deal imminent - French trade.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A deal for further French wheat sales to Iraq is imminent, a senior French grains trader involved in negotiations said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's advancing, it needs some time. But it will be done, imminently,&quot; Bruno Catton, director general of French grains union Sigma, told Reuters at an industry gathering.</p>
<p>French exporters have been negotiating for days to sell more wheat to Iraq following a sale of 300,000 tonnes in December.</p>
<p>Iraq is officially seeking 100,000 tonnes but traders have said the final purchase could cover as much as 325,000 tonnes.</p>
</text>
